1. An LED semiconductor component comprising:

a semiconductor body comprising an active region configured to emit electromagnetic radiation during operation;

a p-contact layer electrically connected to a p-side of the semiconductor body;

an n-contact layer electrically connected to an n-side of the semiconductor body;

a support arranged on a side of the semiconductor body, the support comprising a first via and a second via extending through the support, the first via being electrically connected to the p-contact layer and the second via being electrically connected to the n-contact layer; and

an ESD protection diode arranged between the support and the semiconductor body and electrically connected between the p-contact layer and the n-contact layer,

wherein the ESD protection diode is configured to be reverse-biased during normal operation of the LED semiconductor component and to conduct current in response to an electrostatic discharge voltage applied between the first via and the second via.

1. A flip-chip optoelectronic semiconductor component, comprising:

a semiconductor body (1) having a semiconductor layer sequence (2), the semiconductor layer sequence (2) comprising a p-region (3), an active layer (4) configured to generate or detect electromagnetic radiation, and an n-region (5);

a support (10) on which the semiconductor body (1) is arranged;

a first contact (7) electrically connected to the p-region (3) and a second contact (8) electrically connected to the n-region (5), the first contact (7) and the second contact (8) being arranged for flip-chip mounting of the component;

at least one first via (11) extending through at least part of the support (10) and electrically connected to the first contact (7), and at least one second via (12) extending through at least part of the support (10) and electrically connected to the second contact (8); and

an ESD protection element (15) integrated in or arranged on the support (10), the ESD protection element (15) being electrically connected between the first contact (7) and the second contact (8) via the vias (11, 12) so as to protect the active layer (4) against electrostatic discharge.
